Databases in this state accept no connections. Per Microsoft documentation, the only permitted action on an Inaccessible database is deletion — tier changes and scaling are blocked. These databases cannot be right-sized under this ticket in their current state.

2. Both affected geo servers report lost Key Vault access

vos-iaz-sql-dev-arc11x-geo and geoedserver are configured with customer-managed Transparent Data Encryption. Both display: "Access to Azure Key Vault has been lost for this server."

The key used by arc11x (sqltde in vault bst-iaz-kvt-dev-geo) is Enabled and does not expire until 13/08/2028. Key expiry is therefore not the cause. geoedserver references a different key (TDEProtector/7cb5256d…).

3. vos-iaz-sql-dev-arc11x-geo duplicates an existing environment

It holds the same six databases at identical tiers and capacities as bst-iaz-sql-dev-geo. All six on the bst server are Online and healthy.

4. Cost of the arc11x environment

